THOUGHT: ImageEffect.apply is annotated @Nullable, so it can return null, and its parameter is non-null. The PASS_NULLABLE error likely arises because NullAway infers sprite might be null after the first apply call (since apply can return null), and then that possibly-null sprite is passed into the next effect.apply. To fix this without changing contracts, I should stop applying further effects once sprite becomes null by adding a null check inside the loop and breaking if sprite is null. This keeps the method’s behavior reasonable and satisfies NullAway.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '207,211s/for (final ImageEffect effect : this.getImageEffects()) {
      sprite = effect.apply(sprite);
    }/for (final ImageEffect effect : this.getImageEffects()) {
      if (sprite == null) {
        break;
      }
      sprite = effect.apply(sprite);
    }/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/graphics/animation/AnimationController.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "AnimationController.java" new_build_output.log || true
```

